---
// The viewport frame: a 10px VOID border holding every Obliv1a surface. It is
// the outermost mark of the system, and the only thing that interrupts a
// full-bleed colour region (DESIGN.md §Layout). Fixed rather than a body border
// so the colour regions run under it as the page scrolls.
//
// Pairs with `p-(--frame)` on <body> and the negative inline margin on
// <Section>, which together let a section reach the frame on both sides.
---

<div
  class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 z-50 border-[length:var(--frame)] border-void"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
</div>
